#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:0
msgid ""
"Monitor the state and utilization of your NVIDIA drivers on Ubuntu and "
"resolve common driver issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:7
msgid "Topics: How-to guide Graphics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:11
msgid "Troubleshoot your NVIDIA GPU and drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:13
msgid "You can monitor the state of your NVIDIA GPU and resolve common issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:15
msgid ""
"This guide assumes that you're using the proprietary NVIDIA drivers. Refer "
"to {ref}`install-nvidia-drivers` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:17
msgid "Install NVIDIA monitoring and troubleshooting tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:19
msgid "The following tools are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:21
msgid "`nvidia-bug-report.sh`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:22
msgid ""
"Collects diagnostic information into a compressed report, useful when filing "
"bug reports with NVIDIA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:24
msgid "`nvidia-debugdump`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:25
msgid ""
"Extracts internal GPU debug data, mainly used by NVIDIA support for low-"
"level driver debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:27
msgid "`nvidia-smi`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:28
msgid "Monitors your GPU utilization, memory usage, fan speed and clock speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:30
msgid ""
"For details, refer to [System Management Interface SMI](https://"
"developer.nvidia.com/system-management-interface)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:32
msgid "`nvidia-xconfig`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:33
msgid ""
"Generates the X11 server configuration (`xorg.conf`) for NVIDIA driver "
"settings. Only for legacy Desktop systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:35
msgid ""
"Install the tools from the package matching your driver version. For "
"example, on a Server system using the driver version 535:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:46
msgid "Driver/library version mismatch error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:48
#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:80
msgid ""
"If you encounter the following error when running the `nvidia-smi` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:-1
msgid "Failed to initialize NVML: Driver/library version mismatch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:55
msgid ""
"This typically indicates that the user-space driver packages were upgraded "
"while the kernel module is still on the older version (for example, the "
"client reports one driver version while the kernel module reports another). "
"This situation often occurs after a system upgrade. To verify this, check "
"the kernel logs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:65
msgid "Look for error messages similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:-1
msgid ""
"NVRM: API mismatch: the client has the version 570.172.08, but\n"
"NVRM: this kernel module has the version 570.158.01.  Please\n"
"NVRM: make sure that this kernel module and all NVIDIA driver\n"
"NVRM: components have the same version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:75
msgid ""
"**Solution**: Rebooting the system will load the updated kernel module and "
"bring the versions back in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:78
msgid "No devices were found error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:-1
msgid "No devices were found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:87
msgid ""
"This may occur if the open-source NVIDIA kernel driver [`nouveau`](https://"
"nouveau.freedesktop.org/) is pre-installed and loaded, which conflicts with "
"the proprietary NVIDIA driver. To check whether `nouveau` is loaded:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:97
msgid ""
"**Solution**: If `nouveau` kernel module is loaded, blocklist it and rebuild "
"the `initramfs`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/graphics/troubleshoot-nvidia.md:110
msgid "Then reboot the system for the changes to take effect."
msgstr ""
